# End-of-turn report (mandatory)

After every substantive turn (implementation, ops, review, or investigation), end the user-visible reply with a **Turn Report** using this exact structure. Do not skip it when work was done. For trivial Q&A with no repo/runtime changes, a one-line "No repo/runtime changes" note is enough.

## Turn Report template

```markdown
## Turn Report
- **Goal / request:** …
- **Commit(s):** SHA + subject (or "none")
- **Pushed:** yes/no + remote/branch
- **Deployed:** what was rebuilt/restarted (or "n/a")
- **Runtime verify:** commands + key results (health, gates, counts)
- **Tests:** command + pass/fail counts
- **Files touched:** short list of paths
- **Business / constraints check:** thresholds, secrets, data safety, ML GO claim
- **Blockers / next:** …
```

Be explicit and evidence-based (paste command outcomes, counts, HTTP codes). Prefer linking evidence under `docs/audit/evidence/` when created.
